# MagicTime scheduler series
#
# The patches are generated against the exact AOSP16 commit and are applied
# in this order by ../apply-scheduler-patches.sh.
#
# 0001-walt-eevdf-cass-core.patch
#   Net-adapted scheduler closure from the common ancestor
#   a28b116d7545dd4d5c4b52becfcb803bb135c243 through MagicTime
#   eba8dbd9d11b479cae68918826c344065a6b5d3c. It includes the WALT removal,
#   EEVDF data model/selection, CASS, PELT/uclamp and the final rbtree fix.
#
# 0002-aosp-abi-thermal-platform.patch
#   AOSP16-specific platform/vendor closure: cpufreq/thermal pressure,
#   binder/proc/RMNET callers and the small ABI adaptations required to keep
#   AOSP16 task_struct/cgroup and mm lifetime semantics.
#
# 0003-aosp16-core-api-bridge.patch
#   Bridges scheduler-core calls to the older AOSP16 migration, cpuset,
#   rcuwait, workqueue, cpuidle and smp-call APIs found by the first CI build.
#
# 0004-aosp16-aux-api-bridge.patch
#   Bridges softirq accounting, cpumask iteration and the AOSP16 energy-model
#   API reported by the next CI build.
#
# 0005-aosp16-rbtree-waitqueue-bridge.patch
#   Supplies the cached-rbtree insertion helper and maps the newer waitqueue,
#   kthread and cpuset-DL hooks to their AOSP16 equivalents.
#
# 0006-aosp16-rbtree-erase-bridge.patch
#   Accounts for AOSP16's void rb_erase_cached() return convention.
#
# 0007-aosp16-topology-irqwork-bridge.patch
#   Maps the newer energy-model state query and hard irq_work initializer to
#   their AOSP16 equivalents.
#
# The patches intentionally do not change the stable workflow or defconfig.
# The experimental fragment is appended only by the manual workflow.
